<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Balkan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/1913">1913</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Balkan War was fought from October 1912 to May 1913 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-league">Balkan League</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and Montenegro against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. The allies took almost all Ottoman lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> and Albania, and Albania declared independence. Quarrels over the spoils led directly to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-balkan-war">Second Balkan War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war.jpg" alt="First Balkan War" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avidius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balkanskata_voina_Photobox.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
